```console
$ scherzo-cloud workflow run --help
Run a local command and agent workflow

Usage: scherzo-cloud workflow run [OPTIONS] --source-root <ROOT> --execution-root <PATH> --run-dir <PATH> <WORKFLOW_FILE>

Arguments:
  <WORKFLOW_FILE>  Workflow definition path, resolved from the initial working directory

Options:
      --source-root <ROOT>              Directory boundary for workflow source files
      --execution-root <PATH>           Directory for workflow execution (must already exist)
      --run-dir <PATH>                  Directory to create for this run (must not already exist)
      --prompt-file <PATH>              UTF-8 prompt file, or - to read standard input
      --attachment <MEDIA_TYPE> <PATH>  Append an immutable attachment with its declared media type
      --max-parallel <COUNT>            Maximum simultaneous workflow steps [default: 1]
      --plain                           Force plain human presentation
      --json                            Print the result as JSON
      --color <WHEN>                    Select renderer color behavior [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help                            Print help

Interactive mode:
  Automatic mode uses the terminal interface only when stdin and stdout are terminals,
  TERM is usable, and stdin is not reserved by --prompt-file -. Resize keeps the
  interface active; undersized terminals show a resize notice without changing modes.
  Use Up/Down or j/k to select steps, Enter to inspect logs, ? for complete help,
  Ctrl-C to request cancellation, and q to leave only after publication and cleanup.
  After q, Scherzo restores the terminal and prints the standard plain summary.

```
